warning[dropped_result]: `parse` returns 2 values but this keeps 1; the next value is a `bool`, which usually says whether the call worked
  --> tests/lint/dropped_result/bad.jai:15:14
   |
15 |     value := parse("x");
   |              ^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: receive the flag, or write `, _` to show it is ignored on purpose
   |
14       // The parse failure and the zero it leaves look the same.
15 ~     value, _ := parse("x");
16       total: int;
   |
   = note: `dropped_result` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/dropped_result

warning[dropped_result]: `parse` returns 2 values but this keeps 1; the next value is a `bool`, which usually says whether the call worked
  --> tests/lint/dropped_result/bad.jai:17:13
   |
17 |     total = parse("7");
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: receive the flag, or write `, _` to show it is ignored on purpose
   |
16       total: int;
17 ~     total, _ = parse("7");
18
   |
