warning[dropped_result]: `lookup` returns 3 values but this keeps 2; the next value is a `bool`, which usually says whether the call worked
  --> tests/lint/dropped_result/bad.jai:20:21
   |
20 |     name, number := lookup(2);
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: receive the flag, or write `, _` to show it is ignored on purpose
   |
19       // Two of three values kept; the flag is still dropped.
20 ~     name, number, _ := lookup(2);
21
   |
   = note: `dropped_result` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/dropped_result

